1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:02,800
Year-end dinner. The boss pulls out
a 1 million won bonus envelope.

2
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:02,780
Got a minute?

3
00:00:02,800 --> 00:00:04,100
The phrase I've heard 413 times this year

4
00:00:04,100 --> 00:00:04,600
10 minutes earlier

5
00:00:04,650 --> 00:00:06,400
My turn to give the toast.
My mind went blank.

6
00:00:06,400 --> 00:00:08,750
Then, Hongchaksa from the restaurant:
What do you hear the most?

7
00:00:08,800 --> 00:00:10,000
Got a minute?
09:00, 410th: one more report

8
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:11,200
Got a minute?
17:59, 411th: overtime

9
00:00:11,200 --> 00:00:13,000
23:40, 412th this year:
due tomorrow morning

10
00:00:13,300 --> 00:00:15,580
When I say "Got a minute?", you say "Next year."

11
00:00:15,700 --> 00:00:16,690
Got a minute?

12
00:00:17,950 --> 00:00:18,990
Next year.
The boss shouted the loudest.

13
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:20,100
The room came alive

14
00:00:20,100 --> 00:00:22,290
Just as he handed over the envelope:
Doyun, got a minute?

15
00:00:22,300 --> 00:00:22,900
413th

16
00:00:22,950 --> 00:00:23,680
Next year.

17
00:00:23,700 --> 00:00:24,300
My mouth answered first

18
00:00:24,400 --> 00:00:26,130
Okay, this one's for next year then.

19
00:00:26,150 --> 00:00:27,050
1 million won, pushed to next year

20
00:00:27,050 --> 00:00:28,550
Meanwhile, on the boss's phone:
Director: Mr. Choi, got a minute?

21
00:00:28,820 --> 00:00:30,150
Next year.
The boss too, 389th this year.

22
00:00:30,650 --> 00:00:31,730
Take this one this year.

23
00:00:31,800 --> 00:00:32,850
No reflex this time

24
00:00:32,880 --> 00:00:34,630
One move from Hongchaksa, and you're set.

25
00:00:34,650 --> 00:00:37,650
Habits of speech can bring luck, or chase it away.
Your move for 2027, hongchaksa.kr
